meta {
  name: Create User
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/users
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "first_name": "Test",
    "middle_name": "",
    "last_name": "User",
    "email": "testuser@example.com",
    "role_name": "sales_executive",
    "mobile": "9876543210",
    "manager_id": "{{userId}}",
    "force_password_change": true,
    "send_email_notification": true
  }
}

docs {
  send_email_notification (optional, default true): when true AND the acting
  admin holds admin.team.notify (or rank >= org_admin), identity-service emails
  the new user their login URL + temporary password via communication-service.
  Set false to skip the email. Ignored — no email — if the actor lacks the
  capability, whatever the flag says.

  email is normalized to lowercase and trimmed before it is stored (schema
  1.48.0): "  Test.User@Example.COM " is saved, and returned, as
  "test.user@example.com". The database refuses anything else
  (chk_users_email_lowercase). A second create differing only in case therefore
  now returns 409 "A user with this email already exists." instead of silently
  creating a second account for the same person.
}
